  "summary": "New York State Assembly held a hearing on guidelines for Flock license plate readers, focusing on data sharing and access controls. Local towns like East Greenbush are pursuing stricter rules or bans, with a 'deFlock' vote scheduled for November 18.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "How that information is shared and with who it's being shared; and tangential to that there should be a conversation about who actually has access to that information. It needs to be clearly delineated. It needs to be very tight, and it needs to be auditable",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "We would like East Greenbush to come up with a local law that either bans or extremely restricts this technology altogether.",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "East Greenbush is set to vote on \"deFlocking\" the town on November 18.",
      "paragraph_idx": 16
    }
  ],
